{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a streaming summer. It reads stdin as bytes, splits on newlines, groups each row's val by cat with a dict of float lists, sums each group with math.fsum, and writes sorted 'cat,sum' lines with 2 decimals. It reproduces the public sample out-0 exactly (diff SAME). It is registered as baseline 1.872 (noise 6.2%). Two variants (dropping the rstrip and empty check, and binding dict.get) were not better: medians 1.83 and 1.905 against 1.87, so no win beyond noise. I am resting here rather than spending more energy on changes that the noise cannot resolve.",
